{"availability":"available","full":"douglasmun/TinyOS_enhanced","name":"TinyOS_enhanced","description":"Fully upgraded, security-focused version of the TinyOS hobby OS","category":"Other","language":"C","stars":2,"forks":2,"created":"2026-06-14T04:40:52Z","updated":"2026-10-10T14:36:25Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"","topics":[],"demo":"https://jedisct1.github.io/minisign/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T15:06:20.508Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-10T15:06:20.508Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-10T15:06:20.508Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-10T15:06:20.508Z","stars":2,"forks":2}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A from-scratch, security-focused 32-bit (i386) operating system kernel, written in C and x86 assembly. Boots via Multiboot2/GRUB, runs in QEMU, and demonstrates a full vertical slice of OS concepts — protected mode, PAE paging with NX/W^X, preemptive multitasking, ring-3 user processes, a TCP/IP stack on a real NIC driver, from-scratch cryptography, and ECDSA-signed-ELF secure boot enforced by default.","Successor to douglasmun/TinyOS — substantially expanded in scope, security, and reliability."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/douglasmun/TinyOS_enhanced/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"bb1b768a1db393171635266222804e2c04799f1153192db99d1cd9d59b9847d0","extractedAt":"2026-10-10T15:06:20.679Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T15:06:20.679Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A from-scratch, security-focused 32-bit (i386) operating system kernel, written in C and x86 assembly. Boots via Multiboot2/GRUB, runs in QEMU, and demonstrates a full vertical slice of OS concepts — protected mode, PAE paging with NX/W^X, preemptive multitasking, ring-3 user processes, a TCP/IP stack on a real NIC driver, from-scratch cryptography, and ECDSA-signed-ELF secure boot enforced by default.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/douglasmun/TinyOS_enhanced/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"Boot → shell → login — Multiboot2 boot, first-boot root password setup, PBKDF2-HMAC-SHA256 (100k iterations) password hashing.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/douglasmun/TinyOS_enhanced/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"Ring-3 login shell — login lands in an unprivileged ring-3 shell (35 builtins) that reaches the kernel only through syscalls; password prompts happen in the kernel, so the shell never holds a password. kshell hands over to the kernel shell for networking and security tooling.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/douglasmun/TinyOS_enhanced/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"bb1b768a1db393171635266222804e2c04799f1153192db99d1cd9d59b9847d0","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/douglasmun/TinyOS_enhanced/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-10T15:06:20.679Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-10T14:36:25Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/douglasmun/TinyOS_enhanced/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-10T15:06:20.680Z","hash":"bb1b768a1db393171635266222804e2c04799f1153192db99d1cd9d59b9847d0","originalBytes":11210,"storedBytes":11210,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["shell","boot","doc","kernel","user","build","ring-3","run","security","login","elf","hello.elf","iso","password","qemu","runs","verify","binaries","fail-closed","first","harness","key","license","networking","one","root","signed","syscalls","binary","default","demo","ecdsa","firewall","from-scratch","fuzz","guide.md","harnesses","ids","invariant","kernel.elf","never","pipelines","programs","project","secure","serial","signature","targets","through","unsigned","verdict","against","audit","before","beyond","bit","boots","builtins","comparison","config.md","default.","dist","each","educational","enforcement","file","fully","grub","headless","hobby","holds","int","jobs","kshell","libfuzzer","log","memory","mode","multiboot2","net","net0